{
  "_doc": [
    "Multiplexed parameter groups for the J1939 tab ('Expand Multiplexed PGNs').",
    "A multiplexed PGN carries different messages selected by its first byte(s), so it is split into one row per selector value.",
    "Normal broadcast PGNs (fixed SPN layout) are not listed and are never split.",
    "selector: 'byte' uses data[byte] & mask (optionally >> shift); 'pgn' uses the requested PGN in bytes 1-3;",
    "'isotp' uses the ISO 15765-2 frame type and, for single and first frames, the UDS service identifier.",
    "labels name selector values (decimal keys). 'labels_ref' points to a shared table in 'tables'.",
    "max_rows_per_pgn limits the rows of one PGN and source address; further values share an 'other' row.",
    "Add OEM or implement-specific multiplexers here (e.g. a proprietary PGN with a known first-byte message ID)."
  ],
